## JCL Fundamentals

### Theory: JCL Structure

**JCL Programs contain three types of statements:**

```
1. JOB STATEMENT
   ├─ First statement
   ├─ Defines job name, class, priority
   ├─ Sets accounting and notification
   └─ One per job

2. EXEC STATEMENT
   ├─ Executes a program or procedure
   ├─ Defines program parameters
   ├─ Sets restart conditions
   └─ One or more per job

3. DD STATEMENT
   ├─ Defines data set (file)
   ├─ Maps logical name to physical storage
   ├─ Specifies allocation parameters
   └─ Multiple per EXEC step
```

**Basic JCL Structure:**

```
//JOBNAME JOB parameters
//STEP1   EXEC PGM=PROGRAM-NAME
//SYSOUT  DD SYSOUT=*
//SYSIN   DD *
  data input
/*
//
```

**Syntax Rules:**

```
1. Column positions matter
   ├─ Columns 1-2:   // (statement identifier)
   ├─ Columns 3-8:   Statement name
   ├─ Columns 9:     Blank separator
   ├─ Columns 10-71: Parameters
   ├─ Columns 72-80: Sequence (ignored)
   └─ Column 81+:    Ignored

2. Comments
   ├─ //* starts comment line
   ├─ Can appear anywhere
   ├─ Improve readability
   └─ No computational cost

3. Continuation
   ├─ Parameters exceed column 71
   ├─ Continue on next line
   ├─ Columns 1-2:   //
   ├─ Columns 3-8:   Blank
   └─ Columns 10+:   Continuation parameters

4. Uppercase
   ├─ Keywords must be uppercase
   ├─ Parameters can be mixed
   ├─ Data can be any case
   └─ Good practice: all uppercase
```

**JCL Example with Comments:**

```jcl
//*==================================================
//* PAYROLL PROCESSING JOB
//* Purpose: Calculate monthly payroll
//* Author: HR Systems Team
//* Date: 2024-01-15
//*==================================================
//PAYROLJOB JOB (1234,5678),'PAYROLL RUN',
//             CLASS=A,
//             MSGCLASS=H,
//             NOTIFY=&SYSUID
//*
//* STEP 1: VALIDATE TIMECARD DATA
//*
//VALIDATE EXEC PGM=VALIDATE-TC
//SYSOUT   DD SYSOUT=*
//TCFILE   DD DSN=COMPANY.PAYROLL.TIMECARDS,
//             DISP=SHR
//ERRFILE  DD DSN=COMPANY.PAYROLL.TC-ERRORS,
//             DISP=(NEW,CATLG,DELETE),
//             SPACE=(TRK,(100,50))
//*
//* STEP 2: CALCULATE PAYROLL
//*
//CALC     EXEC PGM=PAYROLL-CALC,COND=(0,NE)
//SYSOUT   DD SYSOUT=*
//EMPFILE  DD DSN=COMPANY.PAYROLL.EMPLOYEES,
//             DISP=SHR
//PAYROLL  DD DSN=COMPANY.PAYROLL.PAYCHECK-OUTPUT,
//             DISP=(NEW,CATLG,DELETE),
//             SPACE=(CYL,(50,25),RLSE)
//*
//* END OF JOB
//
```

