## JOB Statement

### Theory: Job Identification & Control

**JOB Statement Purpose:**

```
JOB Statement tells operating system:
├─ Who submitted job (NOTIFY)
├─ What priority (CLASS)
├─ How to route output (MSGCLASS)
├─ Resource requirements (TIME, REGION)
├─ Accounting information
└─ Job name and identification
```

**Syntax:**

```
//jobname JOB (acct,subacct),'Descriptive Name',
//             REGION=4M,
//             TIME=(0,05),
//             CLASS=A,
//             MSGCLASS=H,
//             NOTIFY=&SYSUID,
//             TYPRUN=SCAN
```

**JOB Statement Parameters Explained:**

```cobol
//PAYROLL JOB (2450,TSK1),'MONTHLY PAYROLL RUN',
//            REGION=8192K,
//            TIME=(0,30),
//            CLASS=A,
//            MSGCLASS=X,
//            MSGLEVEL=(1,1),
//            NOTIFY=USERID1,
//            TYPRUN=HOLD

Parameters:
─────────────────────────────────────────────────

(acct,subacct)
  └─ Accounting information
  └─ Identifies cost center
  └─ First: Account number
  └─ Second: Task/project code
  └─ Example: (2450,TSK1) = Dept 2450, Task TSK1

'Descriptive Name'
  └─ Job description (max 20 chars)
  └─ Visible in output
  └─ Should be meaningful
  └─ Example: 'MONTHLY PAYROLL RUN'

REGION=8192K
  └─ Memory allocation
  └─ K = Kilobytes, M = Megabytes
  └─ Range: 100K to 2G+
  └─ Default: Usually 6M
  └─ Too small → ABEND (abnormal end)
  └─ Too large → System congestion

TIME=(0,30)
  └─ CPU time limit
  └─ Format: (minutes, seconds)
  └─ 0 = Unlimited (if allowed)
  └─ (0,30) = 30 seconds
  └─ (10,0) = 10 minutes
  └─ Exceeded → Job cancelled

CLASS=A
  └─ Job scheduling class
  └─ A-Z and 0-9 valid
  └─ Determines priority
  └─ A = High priority (usually)
  └─ Z = Low priority
  └─ System dependent

MSGCLASS=X
  └─ Message class (output routing)
  └─ A-Z and 0-9 valid
  └─ X = System dependent
  └─ Determines where output goes
  └─ Different classes have different queues

MSGLEVEL=(1,1)
  └─ Message level (what to print)
  └─ Format: (JOB allocation, PROC statements)
  └─ 0 = Nothing
  └─ 1 = Statements and messages
  └─ 2 = All including PROC expansion
  └─ (1,1) = Print JCL and messages

NOTIFY=USERID1
  └─ Who to notify when job ends
  └─ Send email/message to user
  └─ &SYSUID = Current user (special var)
  └─ Useful for job monitoring

TYPRUN=HOLD
  └─ Type of run
  └─ SCAN = Check syntax only
  └─ HOLD = Hold in queue before execution
  └─ COPY = Produce execution JCL only
  └─ Default: Normal execution
```

**Common Job Classes:**

```
CLASS    Priority   Use Case
─────────────────────────────────────
A        High       Critical batch jobs
B        Med-High   Important daily jobs
C        Medium     Standard batch jobs
D        Low        Maintenance jobs
Z        Lowest     Archival, cleanup jobs
```

