## DD Statement

### Theory: Data Set (File) Definition

**DD Statement Purpose:**

```
DD Statement maps logical names to physical datasets:
├─ Defines input/output files
├─ Allocates storage space
├─ Specifies allocation parameters
├─ Manages data set disposition
└─ Routes input/output
```

**Syntax:**

```
//ddname DD DSN=dataset.name,
//           DISP=(status,after-normal,after-abnormal),
//           VOL=SER=volser,
//           UNIT=device,
//           SPACE=(CYL,(primary,secondary)),
//           LRECL=80,
//           RECFM=FB,
//           BLKSIZE=6000
```

**DD Statement Parameters:**

```
DDNAME (Columns 3-8)
  └─ Logical data set name
  └─ COBOL accesses via SELECT...ASSIGN TO
  └─ Examples: SYSOUT, SYSIN, INFILE, OUTFILE
  └─ Max 8 characters

DSN=dataset.name
  └─ Data set name (physical name)
  └─ Hierarchical structure
  └─ Format: NODE.APPLICATION.TYPE.VERSION
  └─ Example: COMPANY.PAYROLL.EMPLOYEE-MASTER.PROD
  └─ Quotes required if mixed case
  └─ & for symbolic substitution

DISP=(status,after-normal,after-abnormal)
  └─ Data set disposition (allocation status)
  
  Status (first parameter):
    NEW       = Creating new dataset
    OLD       = Existing dataset (exclusive)
    SHR       = Share (read-only)
    MOD       = Modify (append)
  
  After-normal (second parameter):
    KEEP      = Keep after successful job
    DELETE    = Delete after job
    CATLG     = Catalog for future use (NEW only)
    UNCATLG   = Remove from catalog
  
  After-abnormal (third parameter):
    DELETE    = Delete if job fails
    KEEP      = Keep if job fails
    CATLG     = Catalog even if fails
    UNCATLG   = Uncatalog even if fails

  Examples:
    DISP=(NEW,CATLG,DELETE)   = NEW file, keep if OK, delete if fails
    DISP=(OLD,KEEP,KEEP)      = Existing, keep regardless
    DISP=(SHR)                = Read-only, existing file

UNIT=device
  └─ Hardware device type
  └─ SYSDA = Direct access (disk)
  └─ TAPE = Tape drive
  └─ 3390 = Disk model number
  └─ 3480 = Tape cartridge
  └─ Default: Usually SYSDA

VOLUME=SER=volser
  └─ Specific volume serial number
  └─ VOL=SER=DISK01 = Use DISK01 volume
  └─ Only if specific volume required

SPACE=(unit,(primary,secondary),release)
  └─ Storage space allocation
  
  Unit:
    CYL = Cylinder (most common, ~500KB on 3390)
    TRK = Track (~14KB)
    BLK = Blocks (variable)
  
  Example: SPACE=(CYL,(100,50),RLSE)
    100 primary cylinders
    50 secondary extents (if needed)
    RLSE = Release unused space at close
  
  SPACE considerations:
    ├─ Too small → Not enough space (ABEND)
    ├─ Too large → Wasted space, high overhead
    └─ Good estimate: Based on data volume

LRECL=length
  └─ Logical record length
  └─ Maximum bytes per record
  └─ Must match program RECORD SIZE
  └─ Example: LRECL=120 (120-byte records)
  └─ LRECL=* for variable length

RECFM=format
  └─ Record format
  └─ F = Fixed length
  └─ V = Variable length
  └─ U = Undefined
  
  Second character:
    B = Blocked
    T = Track overflow (rare)
  
  Third character:
    A = American text (EBCDIC)
    M = Machine (binary)
  
  Examples:
    RECFM=FB    = Fixed Blocked (most common)
    RECFM=F     = Fixed, unblocked
    RECFM=VB    = Variable Blocked
    RECFM=V     = Variable unblocked

BLKSIZE=size
  └─ Block size (bytes)
  └─ Multiple of LRECL for efficiency
  └─ Large BLKSIZE = Better I/O performance
  └─ Example: BLKSIZE=6000 (50 records of 120 bytes)
  └─ Balance with memory usage

DCB=(LRECL=80,RECFM=FB,BLKSIZE=6000)
  └─ Data control block parameters
  └─ Alternative to individual parameters
  └─ All parameters together

SYSOUT=*
  └─ System output routing
  └─ Special DD for output printing
  └─ * = Default output device
  └─ A,B,C = Different output classes
  └─ Usually combined with MSGCLASS

DUMMY
  └─ Dummy data set
  └─ Discards all output
  └─ Used for testing
  └─ Useful for optional input
```

**DD Statement Examples:**

```jcl
//* Input file (existing, shared)
//INPUT    DD DSN=COMPANY.DATA.INPUT,
//             DISP=SHR,
//             UNIT=SYSDA

//* Output file (new, with space allocation)
//OUTPUT   DD DSN=COMPANY.DATA.OUTPUT,
//             DISP=(NEW,CATLG,DELETE),
//             UNIT=SYSDA,
//             SPACE=(CYL,(50,25),RLSE),
//             RECFM=FB,
//             LRECL=120,
//             BLKSIZE=6000

//* Printer output
//PRINT    DD SYSOUT=*

//* Standard input (inline data)
//INPUT    DD *
  input data here
/*

//* Standard error output
//STDERR   DD SYSOUT=*

//* Tape dataset
//BACKUP   DD DSN=BACKUP.DATASET,
//             DISP=(NEW,KEEP),
//             UNIT=TAPE,
//             VOLUME=SER=TAP001,
//             RECFM=FB,
//             LRECL=80

//* Temporary dataset
//TEMP     DD DSN=&&TEMP-DATA,
//             DISP=(NEW,DELETE),
//             SPACE=(TRK,(100,50))

//* Dummy dataset (discard output)
//DUMMY    DD DUMMY
```

