## Data Set Naming Conventions

### Theory: Data Set Hierarchy

**Mainframe Data Set Names:**

```
Format: NODE.APPLICATION.TYPE.SUBTYPE.VERSION

Examples:
  COMPANY.PAYROLL.EMPLOYEE-MASTER.PROD
  COMPANY.PAYROLL.TIMECARD.DAILY
  COMPANY.PAYROLL.PAYCHECK.MONTHLY
  COMPANY.FINANCE.GL.JOURNAL

Naming Standards:
  ├─ Max 44 characters total
  ├─ Periods separate qualifiers
  ├─ Each qualifier max 8 characters
  ├─ Uppercase recommended
  ├─ Descriptive names
  └─ Consistent structure
```

**Data Set Types:**

```
PDS (Partitioned Data Set)
  └─ Like directory with members
  └─ Contains multiple programs/modules
  └─ Format: DSN(MEMBER)
  └─ Example: COBOL.PROGRAMS(PAYROLL)

PDSE (Partitioned Data Set Extended)
  └─ Modern version of PDS
  └─ Better performance
  └─ More members
  └─ Preferred format

Sequential
  └─ Traditional file
  └─ Records in order
  └─ Most common for business data

VSAM (Virtual Storage Access Method)
  └─ Advanced file organization
  └─ Key-based access
  └─ High performance
  └─ Like indexed sequential files
```

**Temporary vs Permanent Data Sets:**

```
Permanent:
  DSN=COMPANY.PAYROLL.MASTER
  ├─ Cataloged in system catalog
  ├─ Persists after job
  ├─ Usually backed up
  └─ High-value data

Temporary (&&):
  DSN=&&TEMP-DATA
  ├─ Automatically deleted
  ├─ Only during job execution
  ├─ Inter-step data passing
  └─ No backup needed

Temporary (SysID.):
  DSN=&SYSUID.PAYROLL.TEMP
  ├─ User-specific temp
  ├─ Uses user ID
  └─ Automatically deleted
```

