## Parameters & Symbols

### Theory: Dynamic JCL with Symbols

**Symbolic Parameters:**

```
JCL Symbols allow dynamic values:
├─ GLOBAL symbols (whole job)
├─ PROC symbols (within procedure)
├─ System symbols (predefined)
└─ Concatenation support

Benefits:
├─ Reuse JCL templates
├─ Avoid hardcoding values
├─ Environment independence
└─ Easy maintenance
```

**System Symbols (Predefined):**

```
&SYSUID      Current user ID
&SYSDATE     Current date (YY.DDD)
&SYSTIME     Current time (HH.MM)
&SYSJOBID    Job ID number
&SYSODDN     Output dataset name
&SYSDSN      Current dataset name
&SYSNODEID   Node ID
&SYSCPU      CPU serial number
&SYSHOST     Host name

Example:
  //PAYROLL JOB (2450),NOTIFY=&SYSUID
  └─ Automatically uses current user
```

**Symbolic Parameters in JCL:**

```jcl
//*==================================================
//* JCL WITH SYMBOLIC PARAMETERS
//*==================================================

//*SET parameters (global symbols)
//SET DSPREFIX=COMPANY.PAYROLL
//SET DOTYPE=.PROD
//SET STEPCLASS=A

//PAYROLJOB JOB (2450),'PAYROLL RUN',
//             CLASS=&STEPCLASS

//* Step 1: Validation
//STEP1 EXEC PGM=VALIDATE
//INPUT   DD DSN=&DSPREFIX.TIMECARD&DOTYPE,
//             DISP=SHR
//OUTPUT  DD DSN=&DSPREFIX.TC-VALID&DOTYPE,
//             DISP=(NEW,CATLG),
//             SPACE=(CYL,(50,25))

//* Step 2: Process
//STEP2 EXEC PGM=CALC,
//           PARM='&DOTYPE'

//* Alternative: SET with string replacement
//SET PREFIX=COMPANY
//SET APP=PAYROLL
//SET ENV=.PROD

//STEP3 EXEC PGM=REPORT
//INFILE DD DSN=&PREFIX..&APP..MASTER&ENV,
//           DISP=SHR
```

**Procedure Symbols:**

```jcl
//* PROCEDURE DEFINITION
//PROCESS PROC INPUTDS=COMPANY.DATA,
//             OUTPUTDS=COMPANY.RESULTS

//STEP1 EXEC PGM=PROCESS-PROGRAM
//IN    DD DSN=&INPUTDS,DISP=SHR
//OUT   DD DSN=&OUTPUTDS,
//           DISP=(NEW,CATLG),
//           SPACE=(CYL,(100,50))

//* INVOKING PROCEDURE WITH PARAMETERS
//MYJOB JOB (2450)
//CALL1 EXEC PROCESS,
//           INPUTDS=COMPANY.INPUT.DATA,
//           OUTPUTDS=COMPANY.OUTPUT.DATA

//CALL2 EXEC PROCESS,
//           INPUTDS=COMPANY.BACKUP.DATA,
//           OUTPUTDS=COMPANY.BACKUP.RESULTS
```

