## Procedures & Templates

### Theory: Reusable JCL Procedures

**Procedure Purpose:**

```
Procedures allow:
├─ Code reuse (DRY principle)
├─ Standardization
├─ Template creation
├─ Simplified job submission
└─ Maintenance efficiency

PROC Library:
├─ Shared JCL procedures
├─ Stored separately from jobs
├─ Included at execution time
└─ System-wide availability
```

**Procedure Definition:**

```jcl
//*==================================================
//* PROCEDURE: PAYROLL-PROCESS
//* Purpose: Standard payroll processing steps
//*==================================================

//PAYROLL PROC INPUTDS=COMPANY.INPUT.DEFAULT,
//             OUTPUTDS=COMPANY.OUTPUT.DEFAULT,
//             DBCLASS=A

//* Step 1: Validation
//VALIDATE EXEC PGM=VALIDATE-PROGRAM,
//              COND=(0,NE)
//SYSOUT   DD SYSOUT=*
//INPUT    DD DSN=&INPUTDS,DISP=SHR
//ERRORS   DD DSN=&OUTPUTDS.ERRORS,
//              DISP=(NEW,DELETE),
//              SPACE=(CYL,(10,5))

//* Step 2: Calculate Payroll
//CALCULATE EXEC PGM=CALC-PAYROLL,
//               CLASS=&DBCLASS,
//               COND=(0,NE)
//SYSOUT   DD SYSOUT=*
//EMPFILE  DD DSN=COMPANY.EMPLOYEES,DISP=SHR
//PAYFILE  DD DSN=&OUTPUTDS.PAYROLL,
//              DISP=(NEW,CATLG),
//              SPACE=(CYL,(100,50))

//* Step 3: Generate Report
//REPORT   EXEC PGM=PAYROLL-REPORT,
//              COND=(0,NE)
//SYSOUT   DD SYSOUT=*
//PAYOUT   DD SYSOUT=*
//PAYROLL  DD DSN=&OUTPUTDS.PAYROLL,DISP=SHR

//* End of procedure
```

**Procedure Invocation:**

```jcl
//*==================================================
//* JOB USING PAYROLL PROCEDURE
//*==================================================

//MYJOB JOB (2450),'MONTHLY PAYROLL'

//* Use procedure with default parameters
//RUN1 EXEC PAYROLL

//* Use procedure with custom parameters
//RUN2 EXEC PAYROLL,
//           INPUTDS=COMPANY.TIMECARDS.WEEKLY,
//           OUTPUTDS=COMPANY.RESULTS.WEEKLY,
//           DBCLASS=B

//* Use procedure multiple times
//RUN3 EXEC PAYROLL,
//           INPUTDS=COMPANY.BACKUP.DATA

//
```

**Procedure Modification:**

```jcl
//* Override DD statements in procedure
//MYJOB JOB (2450)

//RUN EXEC PAYROLL

//* Override INPUT DD from procedure
//VALIDATE.INPUT DD DSN=COMPANY.CUSTOM.DATA,
//                  DISP=SHR

//* Override EXEC parameters
//CALCULATE.PAYFILE DD DSN=COMPANY.CUSTOM.OUTPUT,
//                     DISP=(NEW,CATLG),
//                     SPACE=(CYL,(200,100))

//
```

