## 5. DATA SET NAMING CONVENTIONS

### 5.1 Naming Hierarchy

```
Format: NODE.APPLICATION.TYPE.SUBTYPE.VERSION

Examples:
  COMPANY.PAYROLL.EMPLOYEE-MASTER.PROD
  BANK.ACCOUNTS.TRANSACTION.DAILY.2024-01
  INSURANCE.CLAIMS.MASTER.ACTIVE
  RETAIL.INVENTORY.LOCATION-001.SNAPSHOT

Rules:
  ├─ Max 44 characters total
  ├─ Periods (.) separate qualifiers
  ├─ Each segment max 8 characters
  ├─ Uppercase recommended
  ├─ Use hyphens in segments (not spaces)
  ├─ Descriptive meaningful names
  └─ Consistent structure across organization
```

### 5.2 Data Set Types

```
SEQUENTIAL
  ├─ Traditional file format
  ├─ Records in order
  ├─ Most common for business data
  ├─ Direct access or tape
  └─ Example: PAYROLL.TIMECARD.DAILY

PDS (Partitioned Data Set)
  ├─ Like directory with members
  ├─ Contains multiple programs/modules
  ├─ PDSE = Modern version (preferred)
  ├─ Format: DSN(MEMBER)
  └─ Example: COBOL.PROGRAMS(PAYROLL)

VSAM (Virtual Storage Access Method)
  ├─ Advanced file organization
  ├─ Key-based access
  ├─ High performance
  ├─ Like indexed sequential files
  └─ Example: CUSTOMER.MASTER.VSAM

GDG (Generation Data Group)
  ├─ Time-versioned datasets
  ├─ Automatic versioning
  ├─ Useful for backups
  └─ Example: PAYROLL.BACKUP(+1) for new version
```

### 5.3 Temporary vs Permanent

```
PERMANENT DATASETS:
  DSN=COMPANY.PAYROLL.MASTER
  ├─ Cataloged in system catalog
  ├─ Persists after job ends
  ├─ Usually backed up
  ├─ Contains high-value data
  └─ Long-term retention

TEMPORARY (&&):
  DSN=&&TEMP-DATA
  ├─ Automatically deleted at job end
  ├─ Only during job execution
  ├─ For inter-step data passing
  ├─ No backup needed
  ├─ Cannot pass between jobs
  └─ Saves DASD space

TEMPORARY (User-specific):
  DSN=&SYSUID.PAYROLL.TEMP
  ├─ User-specific temporary
  ├─ Uses user ID in name
  ├─ Automatically deleted
  ├─ Can be shared among user's jobs
  └─ Useful for testing
```

