## 7. CONDITIONAL EXECUTION

### 7.1 COND Statement Theory

**Purpose:** Control whether step executes based on previous step's return code.

```
Concept:
  If (previous-return-code operator value) is TRUE
    Then SKIP this step
  Else EXECUTE this step

Common Patterns:
  ├─ Skip on success
  ├─ Skip on failure
  ├─ Skip on specific errors
  ├─ Multiple conditions
  └─ Step-specific conditions
```

### 7.2 COND Logic Examples

```
SCENARIO 1: Skip if previous succeeded
────────────────────────────────────────
//STEP1 EXEC PGM=VALIDATION
  Returns: 0 (success)

//STEP2 EXEC PGM=ERROR-HANDLER,COND=(0,NE)
  ├─ Condition: (0,NE) = "is return-code NOT EQUAL to 0"
  ├─ RC=0: TRUE → SKIP STEP2
  ├─ RC≠0: FALSE → EXECUTE STEP2
  └─ Meaning: Run only if STEP1 failed

SCENARIO 2: Skip if previous failed
────────────────────────────────────────
//STEP1 EXEC PGM=VALIDATION
  Returns: 8 (error)

//STEP2 EXEC PGM=PROCESS-DATA,COND=(0,EQ)
  ├─ Condition: (0,EQ) = "is return-code EQUAL to 0"
  ├─ RC=0: TRUE → SKIP STEP2
  ├─ RC≠0: FALSE → EXECUTE STEP2
  └─ Meaning: Run only if STEP1 succeeded

SCENARIO 3: Skip on minor errors (run on serious)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//STEP1 EXEC PGM=VALIDATE
  Returns: 4 (warning)

//STEP2 EXEC PGM=SPECIAL-PROCESS,COND=(4,LT)
  ├─ Condition: (4,LT) = "is return-code LESS THAN 4"
  ├─ RC<4: TRUE → SKIP STEP2
  ├─ RC≥4: FALSE → EXECUTE STEP2
  └─ Meaning: Run only if serious error (≥4)

SCENARIO 4: Multi-step condition
────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//STEP1 EXEC PGM=VALIDATE
  Returns: 0 (success)

//STEP2 EXEC PGM=EXTRACT
  Returns: 4 (warning)

//STEP3 EXEC PGM=FINAL,
//           COND=((0,NE,STEP1),(4,LT,STEP2))
  ├─ Skip if: (STEP1=0) AND (STEP2<4)
  ├─ Execute if: (STEP1≠0) OR (STEP2≥4)
  └─ Only runs if either previous had issue
```

### 7.3 Real-World Examples

```jcl
//*==================================================
//* PAYROLL WITH CONDITIONAL STEPS
//*==================================================

//PAYROLL JOB (2450)

//*─────────────────────────────────────────────
//* STEP 1: VALIDATE TIMECARDS
//*─────────────────────────────────────────────
//VALIDATE EXEC PGM=VALIDATE-TIMECARD

//INPUT DD DSN=PAYROLL.TIMECARD.DAILY,DISP=SHR
//OUTPUT DD DSN=&&VALID-CARDS,
//           DISP=(NEW,PASS),
//           SPACE=(CYL,(50,25))
//REPORT DD SYSOUT=*

//*─────────────────────────────────────────────
//* STEP 2: CALCULATE (only if validation ok)
//*─────────────────────────────────────────────
//CALC EXEC PGM=PAYROLL-CALC,
//          COND=(0,NE,VALIDATE)
  └─ Skip if VALIDATE succeeded (RC=0)
  └─ Run only if VALIDATE failed

//INPUT DD DSN=&&VALID-CARDS,DISP=(OLD,PASS)
//OUTPUT DD DSN=&&PAYROLL-DATA,
//           DISP=(NEW,PASS),
//           SPACE=(CYL,(100,50))

//*─────────────────────────────────────────────
//* STEP 3: FORMAT CHECKS (only if calc ok)
//*─────────────────────────────────────────────
//FORMAT EXEC PGM=FORMAT-CHECKS,
//            COND=(0,NE,CALC)
  └─ Skip if CALC succeeded
  └─ Run only if CALC had error

//INPUT DD DSN=&&PAYROLL-DATA,DISP=(OLD,PASS)
//OUTPUT DD DSN=&&CHECKS,
//           DISP=(NEW,PASS),
//           SPACE=(CYL,(100,50))

//*─────────────────────────────────────────────
//* STEP 4: ERROR REPORT (if anything failed)
//*─────────────────────────────────────────────
//ERRORRPT EXEC PGM=GENERATE-ERROR-REPORT,
//              COND=((0,EQ,VALIDATE),
//                    (0,EQ,CALC),
//                    (0,EQ,FORMAT))
  └─ Only runs if ALL previous steps failed

//REPORT DD SYSOUT=*

//*─────────────────────────────────────────────
//* STEP 5: PRINT CHECKS (only if all good)
//*─────────────────────────────────────────────
//PRINT EXEC PGM=PRINT-CHECKS,
//           COND=((0,NE),(0,NE,VALIDATE),
//                 (0,NE,CALC),
//                 (0,NE,FORMAT))
  └─ Only runs if previous steps all ok

//INPUT DD DSN=&&CHECKS,DISP=(OLD,DELETE)
//REPORT DD SYSOUT=*

//
