## 8. PROCEDURES & REUSABLE TEMPLATES

### 8.1 Purpose & Theory

**Procedures** are reusable JCL templates that:
- Standardize job structure
- Reduce code duplication
- Improve maintainability
- Allow parameter customization
- Promote consistency across organization

### 8.2 Procedure Definition

```jcl
//*==================================================
//* PROCEDURE: STANDARD BATCH PROCESS
//*==================================================

//BATCHPROC PROC INPUTDS=DEFAULT.INPUT,
//               OUTPUTDS=DEFAULT.OUTPUT,
//               MEMSIZE=4M

//* Step 1: Validation
//VALIDATE EXEC PGM=VALIDATE-DATA,
//              REGION=&MEMSIZE
//SYSOUT DD SYSOUT=*
//INPUT DD DSN=&INPUTDS,DISP=SHR
//OUTPUT DD DSN=&&VALIDATED,
//           DISP=(NEW,PASS),
//           SPACE=(CYL,(50,25))

//* Step 2: Process
//PROCESS EXEC PGM=PROCESS-LOGIC,
//             REGION=&MEMSIZE,
//             COND=(0,NE,VALIDATE)
//SYSOUT DD SYSOUT=*
//INPUT DD DSN=&&VALIDATED,DISP=(OLD,PASS)
//OUTPUT DD DSN=&OUTPUTDS,
//           DISP=(NEW,CATLG),
//           SPACE=(CYL,(100,50))

//* Step 3: Report
//REPORT EXEC PGM=GENERATE-REPORT,
//             COND=(0,NE,PROCESS)
//SYSOUT DD SYSOUT=*
//DATA DD DSN=&OUTPUTDS,DISP=SHR
//REPORT DD SYSOUT=*

// Pend  ← End of procedure
```

### 8.3 Procedure Invocation

```jcl
//*==================================================
//* JOB USING PROCEDURE
//*==================================================

//MYJOB JOB (2450),'MONTHLY PROCESS'

//* Use procedure with default parameters
//RUN1 EXEC BATCHPROC

//* Use with custom parameters
//RUN2 EXEC BATCHPROC,
//           INPUTDS=COMPANY.CUSTOM.INPUT,
//           OUTPUTDS=COMPANY.CUSTOM.OUTPUT,
//           MEMSIZE=8M

//* Run multiple times with different inputs
//RUN3 EXEC BATCHPROC,
//           INPUTDS=LOCATION1.DATA,
//           OUTPUTDS=LOCATION1.RESULTS

//RUN4 EXEC BATCHPROC,
//           INPUTDS=LOCATION2.DATA,
//           OUTPUTDS=LOCATION2.RESULTS

//

Result:
├─ RUN1: Uses all defaults
├─ RUN2: Custom input/output with 8M memory
├─ RUN3,RUN4: Process different locations
└─ All use same proven procedure logic
```

