## File Management & Operations

### Theory: Data Set Lifecycle

**Typical Lifecycle:**

```
CREATE → PROCESS → BACKUP → ARCHIVE → DELETE

1. CREATE
   └─ Allocate space
   └─ Set attributes
   └─ Catalog if permanent

2. PROCESS
   └─ Read/write data
   └─ Modify as needed
   └─ Generate output

3. BACKUP
   └─ Copy to tape
   └─ For disaster recovery
   └─ Legal requirement

4. ARCHIVE
   └─ Move to slower storage
   └─ Long-term retention
   └─ Compliance

5. DELETE
   └─ When retention expired
   └─ Reclaim space
   └─ Cost reduction
```

