## Error Recovery & Restart

### Theory: Fault Tolerance

**Recovery Strategies:**

```
1. CONDITIONAL EXECUTION
   ├─ COND skips failed steps
   ├─ Prevents cascading failures
   ├─ Each step validates input
   └─ Alternative processing paths

2. RESTART CAPABILITY
   ├─ RESTART=STEPNAME
   ├─ Resume from failure point
   ├─ Skip successful steps
   └─ Saves processing time

3. MANUAL INTERVENTION
   ├─ Error notification
   ├─ Operator investigation
   ├─ Fix root cause
   └─ Resubmit

4. ALTERNATIVE LOGIC
   ├─ Use different program path
   ├─ Lower data quality acceptable
   ├─ Meet time requirements
   └─ Better than failure
```

**Practical Error Handling:**

```jcl
//*==================================================
//* ROBUST ERROR HANDLING JOB
//*==================================================

//ROBUST   JOB (9000,RECOVERY),'ERROR HANDLING',
//             CLASS=A,
//             TIME=(0,120),
//             RESTART=STEP3

//*==================================================
//* STEP 1: PRIMARY PROCESS
//*==================================================

//STEP1    EXEC PGM=PRIMARY-PROCESS

//SYSOUT   DD SYSOUT=*

//INPUT    DD DSN=COMPANY.DATA.INPUT,DISP=SHR

//OUTPUT   DD DSN=&&PROCESS-OUTPUT,
//             DISP=(NEW,PASS),
//             SPACE=(CYL,(500,250))

//ERRORS   DD DSN=COMPANY.ERRORS.PRIMARY,
//             DISP=(NEW,CATLG),
//             SPACE=(CYL,(10,5))

//*==================================================
//* STEP 2: VALIDATE RESULTS
//*==================================================

//STEP2    EXEC PGM=VALIDATE-OUTPUT,
//              COND=(0,NE,STEP1)

//SYSOUT   DD SYSOUT=*

//INPUT    DD DSN=&&PROCESS-OUTPUT,DISP=(OLD,PASS)

//REPORT   DD SYSOUT=*

//*==================================================
//* STEP 3: NORMAL COMPLETION
//*==================================================

//STEP3    EXEC PGM=FINALIZE,
//              COND=(0,NE,STEP2)

//SYSOUT   DD SYSOUT=*

//INPUT    DD DSN=&&PROCESS-OUTPUT,
//             DISP=(OLD,DELETE)

//OUTPUT   DD DSN=COMPANY.DATA.FINAL,
//             DISP=(NEW,CATLG),
//             SPACE=(CYL,(500,250))

//*==================================================
//* STEP 4: IF PRIMARY FAILED - ALTERNATIVE PATH
//*==================================================

//STEP4    EXEC PGM=ALTERNATIVE-PROCESS,
//              COND=(0,EQ,STEP1)

//* Only runs if STEP1 failed (return=0 skip)

//SYSOUT   DD SYSOUT=*

//INPUT    DD DSN=COMPANY.DATA.INPUT,DISP=SHR

//OUTPUT   DD DSN=COMPANY.DATA.FINAL,
//             DISP=(NEW,CATLG),
//             SPACE=(CYL,(300,150))

//FALLBACK DD SYSOUT=*

//*==================================================
//* STEP 5: ERROR NOTIFICATION
//*==================================================

//STEP5    EXEC PGM=SEND-ALERT,
//              COND=((0,EQ,STEP1),(0,EQ,STEP2),OR)

//* Runs if STEP1 OR STEP2 failed

//SYSOUT   DD SYSOUT=*

//MAILTO   DD SYSOUT=*

//

Restart Scenario:
─────────────────

First Run:
├─ STEP1 executes: FAILS (return code 8)
├─ STEP2 skipped (COND failed)
├─ STEP3 skipped (COND failed)
├─ STEP4 executes: SUCCEEDS (alternative path)
├─ STEP5 executes: Sends alert email
└─ Job ends with return code 8

Operator Investigation:
├─ Finds missing input file
├─ Creates missing file
└─ Resubmits with RESTART=STEP1

Resubmission with RESTART=STEP1:
├─ STEP1 executes: SUCCEEDS (input fixed)
├─ STEP2 executes: VALIDATES
├─ STEP3 executes: FINALIZES
├─ STEP4 skipped (COND false - STEP1 succeeded)
├─ STEP5 skipped (COND false - all succeeded)
└─ Job completes successfully
```

